WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.480
T-Bud makes a trekking merchant discoverable and transactable by an AI buyer,

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.440
while keeping each consequential decision with a person.

3
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.880
This is a working Manali booking pilot for Razorpay's AI Growth and

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.275
Agentic Commerce track. The problem is simple: a conversational agent can help

5
00:00:15.275 --> 00:00:19.115
choose a trip, but a recommendation should not silently reserve seats or

6
00:00:19.115 --> 00:00:23.905
authorize a payment. T-Bud makes those boundaries visible, enforceable, and auditable.

7
00:00:24.715 --> 00:00:29.250
Consider four friends planning a two-day, one-night Manali trek, with a total

8
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.320
ceiling of twenty thousand rupees.

9
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.720
They want pickup and upgraded meals.

10
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:38.050
The merchant catalog prices the base trek at sixteen thousand, pickup at

11
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.015
two thousand, and meals at sixteen hundred.

12
00:00:41.105 --> 00:00:44.215
The total is nineteen thousand six hundred rupees.

13
00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:47.415
This landing-page example is labelled illustrative.

14
00:00:47.585 --> 00:00:51.265
The booking interface calls the actual Worker to prepare a fresh quote

15
00:00:51.265 --> 00:00:52.855
from the seeded merchant catalog.

16
00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:55.690
Here is the failure path.

17
00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:59.920
With the same group and add-ons, a nineteen-thousand-rupee ceiling is too low.

18
00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.650
The deterministic policy returns a budget conflict and the exact six-hundred-rupee

19
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:09.805
overage. It does not offer an itinerary approval, reserve capacity, or create

20
00:01:09.805 --> 00:01:13.325
a payment order. The traveller can change the budget or remove an

21
00:01:13.325 --> 00:01:15.715
add-on, then request a new quote.

22
00:01:15.965 --> 00:01:18.995
The failure has a clear explanation and a recovery action.

23
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.580
Restoring the budget to twenty thousand produces an eligible quote.

24
00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.900
Its line items, total, version, departure and expiry are recorded on the

25
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.730
server. The first human gate approves that exact itinerary.

26
00:01:32.205 --> 00:01:35.645
Approval is bound to the quote and the browser session, rather than

27
00:01:35.645 --> 00:01:38.115
a generic permission to buy something later.

28
00:01:38.205 --> 00:01:41.645
An agent can prepare a proposal, but the human must approve the

29
00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:43.555
proposal that will actually be used.

30
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.320
The second gate is a separate decision to hold the seats for

31
00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:52.520
ten minutes. A Cloudflare Durable Object checks capacity atomically, so competing

32
00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.310
agents cannot both claim the same last seats.

33
00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.830
The interface then shows the active hold and remaining availability.

34
00:01:59.495 --> 00:02:01.975
Holding seats still does not authorize payment.

35
00:02:01.975 --> 00:02:05.255
If the hold expires, the flow requires a fresh valid path through

36
00:02:05.255 --> 00:02:07.725
the booking rules before checkout can continue.

37
00:02:10.135 --> 00:02:12.270
Only the third human approval creates a Razorpay order for the approved

38
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:17.870
amount. This pilot uses real Razorpay test-mode APIs, and no real money

39
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.940
is collected. Closing the checkout does not lose the order.

40
00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:26.585
Resume payment checks the server receipt and the active hold, then reopens

41
00:02:26.585 --> 00:02:31.305
the same approved order. Reloading the page also reconciles the receipt before

42
00:02:31.305 --> 00:02:35.535
offering a resume action, rather than trusting stale browser state.

43
00:02:38.265 --> 00:02:40.280
For payment completion, this is a separate sandbox transaction already verified

44
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.680
on the deployed system. Razorpay reported a captured payment of four thousand

45
00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.400
rupees. The signed payment-captured webhook reached T-Bud, and the audit recorded

46
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.750
webhook as the verification source, with the booking confirmed.

47
00:02:53.385 --> 00:02:55.775
Purchased seats become a permanent reservation.

48
00:02:55.945 --> 00:02:59.545
If a late captured payment arrives after capacity is gone, the result

49
00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:03.455
is payment review, with a merchant refund or alternative departure needed.

50
00:03:03.465 --> 00:03:05.055
It is never falsely confirmed.

51
00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:09.550
The architecture separates recommendation from authority.

52
00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:14.760
Workers AI extracts the request and recommends catalog add-ons using validated

53
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:21.045
JSON schemas. Explicit group sizes and total rupee budgets are parsed deterministically.

54
00:03:21.135 --> 00:03:26.325
D1 supplies prices and stores tasks, quotes, approvals and audit records.

55
00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:31.445
Durable Objects own capacity, while the Worker verifies Razorpay payment proofs.

56
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:36.200
A six-person request with pickup and a thirty-thousand-rupee ceiling was verified

57
00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:41.480
live: both AI stages ran, and the catalog total was twenty-six thousand

58
00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:46.795
rupees. A public Agent Card exposes the booking capability through A two

59
00:03:46.795 --> 00:03:50.955
A version one. Web M C P exposes the same tools in

60
00:03:50.955 --> 00:03:55.355
the browser. Both use the same booking handlers, budget rules and human

61
00:03:55.355 --> 00:03:59.425
gates. There is no separate agent shortcut around approvals.

62
00:03:59.435 --> 00:04:03.810
The merchant view makes the protocol surfaces and decision trail inspectable.

63
00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.290
This is the core agentic-commerce contribution: an agent-readable merchant with

64
00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.960
an end-to-end transaction path whose authority stays bounded.

65
00:04:16.705 --> 00:04:18.305
Validation covers sixty-six unit and interface tests, forty-four Worker integration

66
00:04:18.305 --> 00:04:21.655
tests, and seven browser end-to-end tests.

67
00:04:21.985 --> 00:04:26.545
The browser suite checks separate approvals, budget failure, checkout reload

68
00:04:26.545 --> 00:04:29.710
recovery, responsive layouts and accessibility.

69
00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.360
The pilot uses seeded inventory, not a connected tour operator, and payments

70
00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.840
remain in test mode. The next step is operator integration and broader

71
00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:44.182
field validation. The public repository, architecture and live demo are available

72
00:04:44.182 --> 00:04:49.142
for inspection. T-Bud turns an agent's plan into a reviewable booking, one

73
00:04:49.142 --> 00:04:50.732
human decision at a time.
